# L §4.6 steps 2 and 3 (tally 2.1.7 R4, issue #143; F2): a scenario's band table stands above the base's table
# known the same day; the known dates order tables of one layer only. s gives 300.00 PLN at age 8 (under 10), t
# 350.00 PLN; the base keeps 250.00 PLN. 2.1.6's refcore refused each scenario, LOAD-OVERLAP two tables known the
# same day.
=== base.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 2027-12-31
  start 2027-01-01
  end 2027-12-31

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
source act "the act"

band rate(a: int): money PLN
input age: int

version v_act
  cite act
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-12-01
  rate: [0, 6) = 400.00 PLN "under 6"
  rate: [6, 18) = 250.00 PLN "6 to 17"
  age = 8 "the child"

ask b: rate(age) law 2027-06-01
=== s.tally
scenario s over hh
  tally 2
  from 2027-01-01

version vs
  cite act
  governs 2027..
  known 2026-12-01
  rate: [0, 10) = 300.00 PLN "under 10"
  rate: [10, 18) = 200.00 PLN "10 to 17"

ask q: rate(age) in s law 2027-06-01
=== t.tally
scenario t over hh
  tally 2
  from 2027-01-01

version vt
  cite act
  governs 2027..
  known 2026-12-01
  rate: [0, 10) = 350.00 PLN "under 10"
  rate: [10, 18) = 150.00 PLN "10 to 17"

ask qt: rate(age) in t law 2027-06-01
=== expect
b: 250.00 PLN
  law date 2027-06-01, cut 2027-12-31
q: 300.00 PLN
  world: s
  law date 2027-06-01, cut 2027-12-31
qt: 350.00 PLN
  world: t
  law date 2027-06-01, cut 2027-12-31
